What this repository does NOT redistribute
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Simulator aircraft (Laminar Research)
    scripts/build_c182t_package.py produces the "Cessna 182T NAV III (G1000
    CAP)" aircraft by COPYING AND PATCHING Laminar Research's Cessna 172SP,
    which ships with X-Plane 12. It reads that aircraft from the operator's
    own X-Plane installation at build time and writes the result into that
    same installation.

    No Laminar Research asset — .acf, .obj, texture, sound or panel — is
    stored in this repository or distributed with it, and none may be added.
    The build script is a recipe, not a redistribution: running it requires
    a licensed copy of X-Plane 12, and the aircraft it produces is for the
    operator's own use under Laminar's terms, not for onward distribution.

FlightGear C182 exterior (HHS81/c182s)
    The local CAP 487 prototype fetches a pinned GPL-2.0 FlightGear C182 source
    archive after checkout and converts its exterior mesh and textures to
    X-Plane OBJ8. No donor file or generated donor-derived object is stored in
    this Apache-2.0 repository.

    The generated aircraft combines those GPL donor-derived files with files
    copied from the operator's licensed Laminar installation. It is for local
    evaluation and must not be redistributed. The generated package contains
    the donor GPL text, a provenance manifest and a prototype notice. See
    docs/FLIGHTGEAR_C182_GPL_PLAN.md before considering any public release.

Air Manager (Sim Innovations)
    The instruments in instruments/ are original work and run inside Air
    Manager, which each station licenses separately. An Air Manager licence
    is not an Air Player licence; see docs/AM4_COMPAT.md.

    One exception to flag: panels/cap-c182t-mo-station/preview.png and the
    copy inside cap-c182t-mo-station.zip are composites generated by
    panels/cap-c182t-mo-station/generate_assets.py, which pastes in the
    preview image of the STOCK Air Manager G1000 instrument taken from the
    local Air Manager installation. Those two PNGs therefore embed a small
    Sim Innovations asset. They are convenience artifacts and can be
    regenerated; do not treat them as originals.

Equipment documentation (Becker, RHOTHETA, Technisonic, Garmin)
    The faceplates are built from the manufacturers' published manuals. Those
    manuals are copyrighted by their manufacturers and are NOT tracked in this
    repository. docs/SOURCES.md records what each document is and the public
    URL it came from, so anyone rebuilding this work can fetch their own copy
    from the original source.

    Keep it that way. A manual that is useful to have on disk is not thereby
    licensed for redistribution, and this repository is the wrong place to
    mirror one.

    Correction, 2026-09-13 (B1): this paragraph was not true when it was
    written. .gitignore listed the manuals from 65f2c54 onward, but the files
    had been committed before that and were never removed from the index, so
    about 25 MB of Becker, RHOTHETA, Technisonic and Garmin PDFs were tracked
    at HEAD while this file said they were not. They have now been removed
    from the index and remain on disk, ignored, exactly as intended.

    They are still present in the repository's HISTORY. Removing them from
    every commit means rewriting it (git filter-repo) and re-cloning on all
    three machines; that is decision D-4 and has not been done. Until it is,
    this repository must not be shared outside the project.

Civil Air Patrol
    "Civil Air Patrol", "CAP" and the CAP seal and wing emblem belong to the
    Civil Air Patrol. This is a member-built training project; it is not an
    official CAP product and carries no CAP endorsement. Use of the marks
    here is descriptive — identifying the organisation the training is for.

Aviation data
    The flight planner's airport and navaid database is derived from
    OurAirports (public domain). It is NOT FAA NASR data and carries no
    AIRAC cycle guarantee. It is not for real-world navigation.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Not for operational use
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything here is training simulation. The propagation model, the beacon
decodes, the performance tables and the search patterns are calibrated to be
instructive, not to be accurate enough to plan or conduct a real search.
Nothing in this repository may be used for actual flight planning, actual
direction finding, or an actual search-and-rescue mission.
